# Code owners for this workspace.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the repository root, from `docs/`, or from
# `.github/`; it lives at the root, where a person browsing the repository
# sees it next to MAINTAINERS.md. (An earlier revision claimed the
# workspace had no `.github/` directory; since 2026-08-26 it has one,
# carrying FUNDING.yml, the issue templates, and the CI workflows.)
#
# One line, one owner, no exceptions: this project has a single maintainer,
# and MAINTAINERS.md says so plainly rather than implying a team. When a
# second maintainer joins, this file gains a line for the areas they own,
# and MAINTAINERS.md gains a row, in the same change.
#
# An email address is used rather than a GitHub handle deliberately: it is
# the identity that owns the crates.io publishes and the committer identity
# in the history (commits and tags are signed from 2026-08-27 onward —
# see MAINTAINERS.md; history before that date stays unsigned), and it
# does not change if a username does. GitHub only auto-requests a review
# from an email owner when that address belongs to a user with access to
# the repository, which is the case here.

